"Kanban" => "Kanban",
"Id of the tracker the board is a partial representation of" => "ID du formulaire dont le tableau est une représentation partielle",
"Card title field" => "Champ de titre de carte",
"Tracker field containing the inline editable text shown on each card" => "Champ de formulaire contenant le texte modifiable en ligne affiché sur chaque carte",
"e.g. \"kanbanTitle\"" => "par ex. \"kanbanTitle\"",
"Card description field" => "Champ de description de carte",
"Optional text shown below the title on each card" => "Texte facultatif affiché sous le titre de chaque carte",
"e.g. \"kanbanDescription\"" => "par ex. \"kanbanDescription\"",
"Column (state) field" => "Champ de colonne (état)",
"Tracker field representing the columns, usually a dropdown list with options such as \"Wishes\", \"Work\" and \"Done\"" => "Champ de formulaire représentant les colonnes, généralement une liste déroulante avec des options comme \"Wishes\", \"Work\" et \"Done\"",
"e.g. \"kanbanColumns\"" => "par ex. \"kanbanColumns\"",
"Column acceptable values and configuration" => "Valeurs acceptables et configuration des colonnes",
// "For the tracker field mapped in \"column\", defines for each column the value a tracker item must have for that field, as well as the label displayed as the column header and the WiP limit for that column. Implicitely defines the number of columns and in which order they are shown; You can skip values so they are not part of the board (and you typically do, if only to eventually archive done cards).\n\n                The parameter is and array of colon separated values, each containing a coma separated arguments configuring the column.\n\n                In order, the configuration represent the:\n\n                1) Mandatory. The value the mapped field must have in the tracker item for the card to be shown in the matching column.\n                2) Optional. If present and not \"null\", the text to be displayed as the column header instead of the normal tracker field label for the value above. (For example \"Done\" instead of \"Closed\")\n                3) Optional. If present and not \"null\", the WiP (Work in Progress) limit for the cards in the column. In \"null\", there is no limit for the number of cards in the column. Typically you will use null for the first and last column.\n\n                null or nothing between the comas means the parameter is not set. Necessary since the arguments are positional.\n\n                So for example:\n                someValue,someAlternateTextToDisplay,null:someOtherValue,,4\n\n                Means the board would have two colums, the first column would be titled \"someAlternateTextToDisplay\" containing cards with the value \"someValue\" for the mapped field and no limit to the number of cards. The second column would have cards with \"someOtherValue\" for the mapped field, with whatever the label is for that value in the field definition, and the column would be highlighted red if there is more than 4 cards. No card with any other value would be anywhere on the board.\n\n                To allow empty values, include a field with an empty value (ex: someValue:someOtherValue:,Unsorted cards)\n\n                If the whole parameter is absent (not recommended), all possible field values will be used to generate columns (except the empty value).\n\n                " => "For the tracker field mapped in \"column\", defines for each column the value a tracker item must have for that field, as well as the label displayed as the column header and the WiP limit for that column. Implicitely defines the number of columns and in which order they are shown; You can skip values so they are not part of the board (and you typically do, if only to eventually archive done cards).\n\n                The parameter is and array of colon separated values, each containing a coma separated arguments configuring the column.\n\n                In order, the configuration represent the:\n\n                1) Mandatory. The value the mapped field must have in the tracker item for the card to be shown in the matching column.\n                2) Optional. If present and not \"null\", the text to be displayed as the column header instead of the normal tracker field label for the value above. (For example \"Done\" instead of \"Closed\")\n                3) Optional. If present and not \"null\", the WiP (Work in Progress) limit for the cards in the column. In \"null\", there is no limit for the number of cards in the column. Typically you will use null for the first and last column.\n\n                null or nothing between the comas means the parameter is not set. Necessary since the arguments are positional.\n\n                So for example:\n                someValue,someAlternateTextToDisplay,null:someOtherValue,,4\n\n                Means the board would have two colums, the first column would be titled \"someAlternateTextToDisplay\" containing cards with the value \"someValue\" for the mapped field and no limit to the number of cards. The second column would have cards with \"someOtherValue\" for the mapped field, with whatever the label is for that value in the field definition, and the column would be highlighted red if there is more than 4 cards. No card with any other value would be anywhere on the board.\n\n                To allow empty values, include a field with an empty value (ex: someValue:someOtherValue:,Unsorted cards)\n\n                If the whole parameter is absent (not recommended), all possible field values will be used to generate columns (except the empty value).\n\n                ",
"e.g. \"someValue,someAlternateTextToDisplay,null:someOtherValue,,4\"" => "par ex. \"someValue,someAlternateTextToDisplay,null:someOtherValue,,4\"",
"Card relative order field" => "Champ d'ordre relatif des cartes",
"Sort order for cards within a cell.  Must be a numeric field.  You will have to create it if the board represents an existing tracker.  It is not meant to be displayed to the user, or represent something global like \"priority\" (that would make no sense on a partial representation).  It merely means that the card is displayed above any card with lower value, and below any card with a higher one if displayed in the same cell.  When a card is moved board will halve the value of the two surrounding cards to compute the new value" => "Ordre de tri des cartes dans une cellule. Doit être un champ numérique. Vous devrez le créer si le tableau représente un formulaire existant. Il n'est pas destiné à être affiché à l'utilisateur ni à représenter quelque chose de global comme une \"priorité\" (cela n'aurait aucun sens dans une représentation partielle). Il signifie simplement que la carte est affichée au-dessus de toute carte ayant une valeur inférieure, et au-dessous de toute carte ayant une valeur supérieure si elle est affichée dans la même cellule. Lorsqu'une carte est déplacée, le tableau divise par deux la valeur des deux cartes voisines pour calculer la nouvelle valeur",
"e.g. \"kanbanOrder\"" => "par ex. \"kanbanOrder\"",
"Swimlane (row) field" => "Champ de couloir (ligne)",
"Tracker field representing the \"rows\" or \"swimlanes\" of the board. Can be any field with discrete values.  Usually represents a client, a project, or a team member.  \n                \n                By default, all tracker items with that field set to a valid values will be shown on the board. To allow empty values, see swimlaneValues.\n\n                Note:  A kanban board can have multiple rows, but these rows aren't independent, they share the same possible States and Wip limits.  If what you want is completely independent \"rows\", create two boards on the same tracker, with different filters" => "Champ de formulaire représentant les \"lignes\" ou \"couloirs\" du tableau. Il peut s'agir de tout champ avec des valeurs discrètes. Il représente généralement un client, un projet ou un membre d'équipe.  \n                \n                Par défaut, toutes les fiches de formulaire dont ce champ est défini sur une valeur valide seront affichées sur le tableau. Pour autoriser les valeurs vides, voir swimlaneValues.\n\n                Remarque : un tableau kanban peut avoir plusieurs lignes, mais ces lignes ne sont pas indépendantes ; elles partagent les mêmes états possibles et limites WiP. Si vous voulez des \"lignes\" complètement indépendantes, créez deux tableaux sur le même formulaire, avec des filtres différents",
"e.g. \"kanbanSwimlanes" => "par ex. \"kanbanSwimlanes",
"Swimlanes acceptable values and configuration" => "Valeurs acceptables et configuration des couloirs",
"Similar to columnValues, except there is no WiP limit.\n\n                To allow empty values, include a field with an empty value (ex: someValue:someOtherValue:,Unsorted cards).  An aditional swimlane will be included for empty values.\n\n                If the parameter is present but only contains the empty value (ex: ,Unsorted cards), all possible field values will be used to generate swimlanes, and an aditional swimlane will be included for empty values.\n                " => "Similaire à columnValues, sauf qu'il n'y a pas de limite WiP.\n\n                Pour autoriser les valeurs vides, incluez un champ avec une valeur vide (ex. : someValue:someOtherValue:,Unsorted cards). Un couloir supplémentaire sera inclus pour les valeurs vides.\n\n                Si le paramètre est présent mais ne contient que la valeur vide (ex. : ,Unsorted cards), toutes les valeurs possibles du champ seront utilisées pour générer les couloirs, et un couloir supplémentaire sera inclus pour les valeurs vides.\n                ",
"e.g. \"someValue,someAlternateTextToDisplay:someOtherValue\"" => "par ex. \"someValue,someAlternateTextToDisplay:someOtherValue\"",
"The tracker field \"%0\" selected in parameter is configured to allow multiple values. This is not mappable in a kanban board" => "Le champ de formulaire \"%0\" sélectionné en paramètre est configuré pour autoriser plusieurs valeurs. Il n'est pas mappable dans un tableau kanban",
"The tracker field \"%0\" selected in parameter is of a type that is not enumerable" => "Le champ de formulaire \"%0\" sélectionné en paramètre est d'un type qui n'est pas énumérable",
"Column value \"%0\" specified in parameter \"%1=%2\" is not found in tracker field \"%3\".  Possible values are %4" => "La valeur de colonne \"%0\" spécifiée dans le paramètre \"%1=%2\" est introuvable dans le champ de formulaire \"%3\". Les valeurs possibles sont %4",
"Empty values" => "Valeurs vides",
"Wip limit value \"%0\" specified in parameter \"%1=%2\" is not numeric" => "La valeur de limite WiP \"%0\" spécifiée dans le paramètre \"%1=%2\" n'est pas numérique",
